ASYNC TCP PORT SCANNER IN C++
=============================

What it is
  A fast, single-threaded TCP port scanner for Linux written in C++17.
  It starts many non-blocking connections at once and waits for all of them
  with poll(), then reports open ports, closed and filtered counts, scan time
  and speed (ports per second).

Requirements
  Linux (Kali, Ubuntu, Debian, or WSL on Windows) and g++.
  Install g++ if needed:  sudo apt install g++

Build
  g++ -std=c++17 -O2 -o scanner scanner.cpp

Run
  ./scanner --demo
      Built-in self test. The program creates its own open ports, scans
      ports 1-10000 and prints PASS if every port was detected.

  ./scanner 127.0.0.1 -p 1-10000
      Scan ports 1-10000 on the given host.

  ./scanner 127.0.0.1 -p 1-1024 -c 500 -t 300
      -p start-end   port range (default 1-1024)
      -c number      connections started at once, 1-900 (default 200)
      -t milliseconds  timeout for each batch (default 800)

Expected demo output (end)
  RESULT: PASS - scanner detected every open port

Files
